{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed56627177/9/codegen_prompts/6.md\"","aggregated_output":"你要为一个新的 ARC-AGI 风格题目实现代码。代码文件必须包含 `main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray` 和 `generate_input() -> np.ndarray`。\n\n## 新题位置\n\n- 描述目录：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed56627177/9`\n- 题号：`6`\n- 目标代码路径：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed56627177/9/6.py`\n\n## 新题描述\n\n<new_puzzle index=\"6\">\n- `description`：根据网格边缘色带的颜色顺序，对网格内部的同心矩形嵌套图案进行颜色层级重排。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为一种主色（如 black）。\n  - 网格中央有一个由多种颜色组成的同心矩形嵌套图案：最外层是一种颜色的单像素宽矩形框，内部是另一种颜色的矩形框，依此类推，最内层可能是一个实心小矩形。每层颜色各不相同。\n  - 网格的最上方一行（或最左方一列）有一排单像素色带，从左到右（或从上到下）依次排列若干颜色，这些颜色恰好是同心矩形中出现的所有颜色，但顺序与同心矩形中从外到内的顺序不同。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 读取边缘色带中颜色的排列顺序，从左到右记为 C1, C2, C3, ...\n  - 在原始同心矩形中，识别每层矩形框的颜色及其层级（从外到内）。\n  - 重新构建同心矩形：最外层使用 C1 的颜色，第二层使用 C2 的颜色，依此类推。每层保持单像素宽矩形框的形状，嵌套结构与原始图案的层数和几何比例完全相同，仅颜色重新分配。\n  - 边缘色带本身在输出中保持不变。\n\n- `Key insight`：同心矩形的层级结构是\"骨架\"，色带是\"重排指令\"。解题者需要先识别出同心矩形的层级顺序，再发现色带编码了新的颜色分配映射——色带的第 k 个颜色映射到第 k 层，而不是映射到某个特定颜色。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n## 机制相似参考题\n\n下面参考题由本地相似度流程自动选择：先用 `annotations`/docstring/代码特征抽取机制标签，再按机制相似度、文本相似度和代码特征相似度重排，并用 MMR 做去重。优先学习这些题的对象识别方式、随机生成器约束、边界条件处理，不要照搬旧题规则。\n\n已选参考：train/34cfa167, train/22208ba4, train/db118e2a, train/52364a65, eval/581f7754, train/a834deea, train/d749d46f, eval/8f215267\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"1\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"34cfa167\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3731\nmechanism=0.4564\nlexical=0.0135\ncode_feature=0.5000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, object:frame, object:rectangle, operation:sort_order, output:same_size, relation:direction, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/34cfa167.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/34cfa167.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nComplete a four-corner framed rectangle from one decorated anchor rectangle and its diagonal mate.\n\nInput structure:\n- The background is the dominant color.\n- Two same-color solid rectangular anchors of the same size sit on opposite\n  diagonal corners, with the first anchor above-left of the second.\n- The upper-left anchor has two one-cell-thick vertical control bars to its\n  right and two one-cell-thick horizontal control bars below it.\n\nRule:\n- Copy the anchor rectangle into the two missing corners of the implied\n  larger rectangle.\n- Repeat the right-side control bars horizontally between the left and right\n  anchors, using their spacing as the period, and draw the outer top and\n  bottom borders in the first right-control color.\n- Repeat the below-side control bars vertically between the top and bottom\n  anchors, using the same period, and draw the outer left and right borders\n  in the first below-control color.\n\nKey insight: The small control bars are the first two ticks of two periodic\nframe patterns; the diagonal anchor supplies the opposite corner and the\nmissing two anchor copies.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"symmetry/pattern\",\n  \"src\": \"two same-color solid rectangular anchors, with two right control bars and two below control bars beside the upper-left anchor\",\n  \"dst\": \"the missing two anchor corners and periodic frame segments between all four anchors\",\n  \"transform\": \"copy the anchor rectangle into the missing corners; repeat the right-control colors across the top and bottom anchor rows and outer borders, and repeat the below-control colors down the left and right side bars using the same spacing\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"2\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"22208ba4\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3660\nmechanism=0.4460\nlexical=0.0136\ncode_feature=0.5000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, object:frame, object:grid_edge, object:rectangle, object:sprite, operation:sort_order, output:same_size, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/22208ba4.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/22208ba4.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nMove the repeated boundary color's rectangles one block inward while leaving singleton boundary rectangles in place.\n\nInput structure:\n- The background is the most common color.\n- Foreground objects are solid monochrome rectangles touching a grid corner.\n- Exactly one foreground color appears as multiple separate 4-connected objects; other colors appear once.\n\nRule:\n- Clear the multiple objects of the repeated color from their original positions.\n- For each cleared rectangle, translate it away from the row and column border it touches by exactly its height and width.\n- Keep singleton-color objects unchanged; overlapping translated rectangles of the same color merge.\n\nKey insight:\n- Multiplicity selects the moving color, and each boundary rectangle's touched edges determine its inward diagonal translation.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_along_path\",\n  \"src\": \"the foreground color with multiple 4-connected solid rectangles on grid corners\",\n  \"path\": \"from each rectangle's corner, move inward away from the touched row and column borders by one rectangle height/width\",\n  \"trajectory\": \"translate each selected rectangle once; same-color overlaps merge\",\n  \"transform\": \"clear selected rectangles at their original positions; leave singleton-color rectangles unchanged\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"3\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"db118e2a\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3556\nmechanism=0.4746\nlexical=0.0140\ncode_feature=0.2500\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, object:frame, object:rectangle, object:sprite, operation:sort_order, relation:direction, relation:inside\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/db118e2a.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/db118e2a.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nNormalize the framed input motif into a 5x5 icon and stamp two copies on a 15x15 canvas.\n\nInput structure\nThe input is a rounded rectangular frame: the four corners are the background\ncolor, and every other outer-border pixel has one frame color. Non-background\npixels inside that frame are the motif to preserve.\n\nRule\nMake a 5x5 version of the rounded frame with a 3x3 interior. Crop the input\ninterior motif to its bounding box, center that crop in the 3x3 interior, and\npaste the resulting 5x5 icon at upper-left positions (2, 2) and (8, 8) in a\n15x15 background canvas.\n\nKey insight\nThe variable-size frame is only a carrier; the meaningful object is the\ncompact interior motif, which is normalized to the fixed 3x3 icon interior.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"transform_in_place\",\n  \"src\": \"rounded rectangular outer frame with a non-background interior motif\",\n  \"transform\": \"build a 5x5 rounded-frame icon from the frame color, center the interior motif bbox in its 3x3 interior, and paste two copies at fixed diagonal positions on a background canvas\",\n  \"grid_shape\": \"15x15\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"4\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"52364a65\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3427\nmechanism=0.4291\nlexical=0.0145\ncode_feature=0.4000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, object:grid_edge, object:sprite, output:same_size, relation:direction, relation:inside, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/52364a65.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/52364a65.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nErase the two leftmost columns of every foreground object, leaving the rest of each object in place.\n\nInput structure:\n- A grid has one dominant background color and several monochromatic 4-connected foreground objects.\n- Each foreground object spans at least two columns in its bounding box.\n\nRule:\n- Find each same-color 4-connected foreground object.\n- Within each object's own bounding box, set foreground pixels in the two leftmost columns to the background color.\n- Leave all other pixels unchanged.\n\nKey insight:\n- The deletion is measured from each object's local left edge, not from the grid edge or from a shared global column.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"transform_in_place\",\n  \"src\": \"monochromatic 4-connected foreground objects on a background\",\n  \"transform\": \"for each object, set foreground pixels in its two leftmost bbox columns to bg\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"5\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"581f7754\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3532\nmechanism=0.4565\nlexical=0.0142\ncode_feature=0.3333\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, object:frame, object:grid_edge, object:sprite, operation:sort_order, relation:direction, relation:inside, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/581f7754.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/581f7754.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nSlide multi-color sprites to align their marker pixels with matching isolated border anchors.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most common color.\n- Multi-color sprites in the interior; each has a minority-color \"marker\" pixel.\n- Isolated border pixels (non-bg with all 4-neighbors bg) act as anchors.\n\nRule:\n- Match each sprite to the border anchor sharing its marker color.\n- Top/bottom-edge anchor (non-corner): slide sprite horizontally so marker column = anchor column.\n- Left/right-edge anchor (or corner): slide sprite vertically so marker row = anchor row.\n\nKey insight: The anchor's edge position determines the slide axis — top/bottom means horizontal, left/right (or corner) means vertical.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_to_match\",\n  \"src\": \"multi-color sprite s with a unique marker color (minority color inside s)\",\n  \"dst\": \"align to isolated border pixel d (same marker color)\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"s.marker.color == d.color\",\n  \"transform\": \"translate s: if d on top/bottom edge → align col(s.marker) to col(d); else → align row(s.marker) to row(d); clip out-of-bounds pixels\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"6\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"a834deea\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3349\nmechanism=0.3993\nlexical=0.0169\ncode_feature=0.5000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, object:frame, object:sprite, operation:sort_order, output:same_size, relation:inside\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/a834deea.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/a834deea.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nFill each black 5x5 region's missing interior positions with a fixed 3x3 positional color legend.\n\nInput structure\n- The grid uses teal as the dominant background and black for one or more\n  5x5 regions.\n- Each black region has a black one-pixel border and a 3x3 interior that\n  may already contain teal pixels.\n\nRule\n- Overlay the legend 1 7 6 / 4 8 5 / 2 9 3 on the 3x3 interior of every\n  5x5 black region.\n- Wherever an interior non-center legend position is still black, recolor it\n  to the corresponding legend color; leave existing teal pixels, the center,\n  and the black border unchanged.\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
